From d15ff601ba7bfb5d6844f1c97db59be3d4562806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 21:02:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the public CLI and skill release pipeline

Port the reviewed distribution pipeline from the integration branch onto
main's CLI (doctor, init, upload, publish, guarded go, connect, local stdio
mcp) so the CLI can ship as the npm package live-link and the public skill
repository Melade-Inc/live-link-skill.

- scripts/release: esbuild bundle of packages/cli into one dependency-free
  ESM file; bundle input audit that admits only the named owned sources and
  files of eight reviewed third-party packages (Zod 3.25.76, the MCP SDK
  1.30.0 and its schema dependencies), each pinned by version, license and
  license-file SHA-256; public tree builder (skill, publish.sh/connect.sh
  wrappers, installer, VERSION, publish workflow); offline tree verifier;
  read-only published-package inspector.
- packages/cli: Node gate before any import (22.12.0; main's CLI has no
  node:sqlite), version constant, Apache-2.0 metadata, LICENSE, NOTICE and a
  composed THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES; doctor now reports cliVersion, nodeSupported
  and credentialSource.
- packages/agent-kit: distribution describes package, version, node floor,
  skill and install command; cliCommand() is null while unpublished and every
  guide renders its honest variant from that state; renderGuide accepts a
  registry override for tests.
- CI runs tests/ops; release-cli.yml builds, verifies and pushes the public
  tree on a cli-v* tag. Runbook in docs/operations/CLI_RELEASE.md.

Verified on Node 24.21: workspace typecheck, eslint --max-warnings 0, 249
unit tests, 20 CLI process tests, 45 ops tests, both production builds; the
offline dry run passes (16 public files, 6 package files, 881,780-byte
bundle, no runtime imports outside node:*). Discovery stays unpublished;
no npm publication, tag or hosted change.

