@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# Public CLI and skill release
+
+Ships the reviewed `packages/cli` as the npm package `live-link` and the public skill repository
+`Melade-Inc/live-link-skill`, then flips discovery to `published`. Source: `scripts/release/`,
+`.github/workflows/release-cli.yml`, the generated `.github/workflows/publish.yml` in the public tree.
+Offline evidence and limits: [DISTRIBUTION_DRY_RUN.md](DISTRIBUTION_DRY_RUN.md).
+
+## One-time setup (Ryan)
+
+1. npm account with 2FA. As of 2026-09-16 the name `live-link` is unclaimed (registry 404); the first
+   publish claims it. Fallback name if that changes: `@melade/live-link` (update `packageName` in
+   `scripts/release/build-cli.mjs` and the tarball URL in `verify-distribution.mjs`).
+2. Public repository `Melade-Inc/live-link-skill`, empty, default branch `main`. It must be public:
+   `npx skills add` on a private repository needs the reader's own GitHub auth.
+3. Secrets, never in git:
+   - `DISTRIBUTION_REPO_TOKEN` in `Melade-Inc/live-link`: fine-grained token, `contents: write` on
+     `Melade-Inc/live-link-skill` only. Used by `release-cli.yml` to push the generated tree and tag.
+   - `NPM_TOKEN` in `Melade-Inc/live-link-skill`: npm granular access token with publish rights for
+     `live-link`, or configure npm trusted publishing for that repository's `publish.yml` and drop the
+     token. Used by the generated `publish.yml` (`npm publish --provenance --access public`).
+4. Optional: install the Claude GitHub App on the skill repository so reviews can read it.
+
+## Release
+
+From `main` at the reviewed commit, with `packages/cli/package.json` and `packages/cli/src/version.mjs`
+agreeing on the pin:
+
+```sh
+pnpm release:build
+node scripts/release/verify-distribution.mjs --dry-run dist/distribution     # must print ok: true
+git tag cli-v0.1.0 && git push origin cli-v0.1.0
+```
+
+`release-cli.yml` rebuilds and re-verifies on the runner, then pushes the tree and tag `v0.1.0` to the
+skill repository. Its `publish.yml` verifies every file hash and mode again, smoke-tests the bundle,
+and publishes to npm with provenance. A tag that already exists in the skill repository fails the
+release; bump the pin instead of re-tagging.
+
+## Verify the published release
+
+```sh
+node scripts/release/verify-distribution.mjs 0.1.0            # npm metadata, tag, skill, notices, tarball bytes
+npx -y live-link@0.1.0 doctor                                  # from a clean container, no repository checkout
+npx skills add Melade-Inc/live-link-skill --skill live-link --list
+```
+
+All three must pass before the flip.
+
+## Flip discovery to published
+
+Merge the prepared "publish CLI discovery" change: `registry.distribution` becomes
+`{ status: 'published', version: '0.1.0', install: 'npx -y live-link@0.1.0', skill: 'npx skills add …' }`,
+`Public CLI installation` leaves the `unavailable` list, and CI gains the `published-cli` job that runs
+the pinned package from the registry. Deploy management; confirm `https://live.link/start.md` and
+`/.well-known/agent.json` show the install command. The flip PR cannot merge before publication: its
+CI job fails while the pin is not on npm.
+
+## Rollback
+
+Never `npm unpublish` after the first 72 hours. `npm deprecate live-link@0.1.0 "<reason>"`, revert the
+flip PR so guides render the unpublished variant again, deploy management. The skill repository tag
+stays as history.
+
+## Next version
+
+Bump `packages/cli/package.json` and `packages/cli/src/version.mjs` together, re-run the dry run, tag
+`cli-v<version>`, verify, then update `registry.distribution.version` and `install` in the same PR that
+records the verification.
